1000:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * system call (or maximum API call) interrupt priority.  Interrupts that are
1001:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * above the maximum system call priority are kept permanently enabled, even
1002:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * when the RTOS kernel is in a critical section, but cannot make any calls to
1003:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * FreeRTOS API functions.  If configASSERT() is defined in FreeRTOSConfig.h
1004:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * then portASSERT_IF_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY_INVALID() will result in an assertion
1005:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * failure if a FreeRTOS API function is called from an interrupt that has been
1006:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * assigned a priority above the configured maximum system call priority.
1007:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * Only FreeRTOS functions that end in FromISR can be called from interrupts
1008:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * that have been assigned a priority at or (logically) below the maximum
1009:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * system call interrupt priority.  FreeRTOS maintains a separate interrupt
1010:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * safe API to ensure interrupt entry is as fast and as simple as possible.
1011:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * More information (albeit Cortex-M specific) is provided on the following
1012:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * link: https://www.FreeRTOS.org/RTOS-Cortex-M3-M4.html */
