1177:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****     /* RTOS ports that support interrupt nesting have the concept of a maximum
1178:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * system call (or maximum API call) interrupt priority.  Interrupts that are
1179:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * above the maximum system call priority are kept permanently enabled, even
1180:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * when the RTOS kernel is in a critical section, but cannot make any calls to
1181:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * FreeRTOS API functions.  If configASSERT() is defined in FreeRTOSConfig.h
1182:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * then portASSERT_IF_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY_INVALID() will result in an assertion
1183:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * failure if a FreeRTOS API function is called from an interrupt that has been
1184:/home/zz/quard-start/Quard-Star/trusted_domain/FreeRTOS-Kernel/queue.c ****      * assigned a priority above the configured maximum system call priority.
